& [Objective]
  + promote the smallest useful read-only query nucleus from live cantor_scribe as a separate effect-free in-memory Cantor kernel component
  + discover units deterministically inside an already-complete supplied-project assembly without storage indexes or host access

& [Requirements]
  + [CIMF-001] preserve dictated source and exact selected live and predecessor byte identities before derived formation or Rust implementation
  + [CIMF-002] use published bookend b31ee13cd4246f5be73d64bdaa68baf5357a601c as predecessor
  + [CIMF-003] do not modify delete stage normalize copy or otherwise disturb the live C checkout
  + [CIMF-004] implement a separate safe-Rust workspace crate named cantor_sop_query
  + [CIMF-005] accept only an already-supplied ProjectAssemblyResult and a strict in-memory FindRequest
  + [CIMF-006] refuse incomplete diagnostic-bearing malformed or tampered project assemblies before lookup
  + [CIMF-007] independently replay the semantic manifest snapshot generation assembly envelope and assembly result digest
  + [CIMF-008] support Unicode-lowercase lexical exact and prefix matching over unit labels and aliases without normalization fuzzy ranking or semantic-equivalence claims
  + [CIMF-009] optionally filter by unit namespace visible package dependency closure kind context scope purpose perspective validity instant and superseded status
  + [CIMF-010] preserve ambiguity and return one hit per unit using the lexically least matching key
  + [CIMF-011] order hits deterministically by matched key then unit identity independent of source vector order
  + [CIMF-012] enforce at most4096 query-text bytes at most128 kind filters 1..1000 page size at most4096 bytes per context filter and at most1MiB request machine form
  + [CIMF-013] refuse unknown request fields duplicate semantic set members invalid profiles malformed identifiers unknown visibility roots and unknown kinds
  + [CIMF-014] provide deterministic pagination with no duplicate boundary records and a sealed cursor bound to snapshot generation query filters and continuation coordinate
  + [CIMF-015] distinguish stale-generation cursor refusal from changed-query or tampered-cursor refusal
  + [CIMF-016] produce a domain-separated query digest and sealed result digest bound to the assembly result
  + [CIMF-017] validate find results by deterministic replay and refuse result or request tampering
  + [CIMF-018] bind capability kernel.sop.semantic-find through the instance contract while retaining the whole cantor_scribe candidate as held
  + [CIMF-019] statically exclude filesystem path APIs process environment SQLite database async transport LSP MCP network provider CLI unsafe mutation and live-effect surfaces
  + [CIMF-020] test constructive ambiguity aliases literal metacharacters filters context validity visibility pagination order independence and replay
  + [CIMF-021] test adversarial incomplete and tampered assembly budgets identities machine forms filters cursors and result tampering
  + [CIMF-022] independently verify the five selected source files still match recorded roots path byte count and SHA256
  + [CIMF-023] verify focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy format exact workspace cross-host script parsing recursive evidence and git attribution gates
  + [CIMF-024] publish only owned source formation implementation tests evidence and intentional transitive manifests
  + [CIMF-025] retain filesystem loading SQLite storage indexes search ranking neighborhood completion rule evaluation references drafts revision LSP MCP transport provider model execution and live service operation as unresolved separately governed candidates

& [Acceptance]
  + [CIMF-A01] source justification plan solution matrix phase lock and satisfaction signature cross-bind exactly
  + [CIMF-A02] selected-source custody independently replays from the unchanged live checkout and exact predecessor commit
  + [CIMF-A03] focused constructive adversarial static-absence and fresh-process query gates pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [CIMF-A04] exact workspace Clippy format dual-host script parse recursive evidence and protected-live-state checks pass before publication
  + [CIMF-A05] integration evidence promotes only kernel.sop.semantic-find while whole cantor_scribe and every excluded authority remain held

& [NonAuthority]
  + query input and output are supplied values only and grant no host path storage execution installation model provider operator transport remote mutation update publication or external-effect authority
  + successful lookup proves bounded lexical correspondence inside one validated snapshot and does not prove truth relevance intent authorization or actionability
